Mission

Transform GitHub Digest from “top repos by total stars” into a daily discovery briefing that:

surfaces new-to-you and rising repos (not just mega-projects),

shows summaries for selected repos,

refreshes automatically on a schedule,
while preserving the existing fetch flow and today-board semantics.

Non-negotiable invariants (do not violate)

Do not rewrite the fetch flow. Keep the current fetch steps and meaning of repo_searches.last_seen_at.

“Today board” must continue to mean: repos with repo_searches.last_seen_at = today (current UI logic).

DB remains SQLite at the same path; existing tables and fields must not be renamed or removed.

All new work must be additive: new columns/tables, new query paths, new CLI command(s), new scheduled job(s).

All changes must be backed by:

schema migration(s),

unit tests (query logic),

at least one end-to-end smoke test (fetch → summarize → board renders).

Current baseline (assumed true)

Fetch flow:

Load saved searches from config/saved_searches.json

For each search, call GitHub Search Repositories (sorted by stars)

Upsert each repo into repos by github_id (update fields + set last_seen_at)

Record repo/search association in repo_searches with its own last_seen_at

Record run in runs with status and counts

Refreshing = re-running github-digest fetch.

UI “today board” filters by repo_searches.last_seen_at = today.

Preserve all this.

Deliverables (must produce all)
D1. Database migrations (idempotent / safe)

Add first_seen_at column to repos (DATETIME/TEXT ISO8601).

Create table repo_stats_daily to track daily stars (and optionally forks/issues).

Create table repo_summaries to store generated summaries and metadata.

D2. Fetch enhancement (minimal)

At the end of each fetch, write one repo_stats_daily row per seen repo for “today”.

Must not increase API calls beyond current Search calls (no README fetch inside fetch).

D3. New board modes + queries

Add board sections (or toggles):

New-to-you: first seen recently (default 7 days)

Rising: stars gained (default 7 days delta)

Updated: recent pushed, but with “anti-giant” filters (configurable)

Default page should prioritize discovery modes, not all-time stars.

D4. Summarization pipeline (separate command)

Add CLI command: github-digest summarize

Summarize only eligible repos (defined below), store results in repo_summaries.

Summary must appear on UI for those repos.

D5. Scheduling

Provide systemd timers (preferred) or cron examples:

fetch every 2 hours

summarize once daily (or twice) with daily cap

D6. Quality gates & tests

Unit tests for:

first_seen_at behavior,

rising delta computation,

eligibility selection & daily cap,

idempotency (summarize doesn’t re-summarize unchanged repos).

One E2E smoke test:

run fetch on fixture data,

run summarize,

verify UI query returns items with summaries.

Schema spec (exact)
1) repos table: add column

first_seen_at TEXT (ISO8601 string)
Rules:

On insert: set first_seen_at = now

On upsert update: never overwrite first_seen_at

2) repo_stats_daily
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS repo_stats_daily (
  repo_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
  date TEXT NOT NULL,              -- YYYY-MM-DD
  stars INTEGER NOT NULL,
  forks INTEGER,
  open_issues INTEGER,
  PRIMARY KEY (repo_id, date),
  FOREIGN KEY (repo_id) REFERENCES repos(id)
);
3) repo_summaries
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS repo_summaries (
  repo_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  summary TEXT NOT NULL,
  why_interesting TEXT NOT NULL,
  tags TEXT NOT NULL,              -- JSON array as string
  model TEXT,
  source TEXT NOT NULL,            -- e.g. "metadata" or "readme"
  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL,         -- ISO8601
  FOREIGN KEY (repo_id) REFERENCES repos(id)
);
Discovery logic spec (exact)
A) “New-to-you” selection

Definition:

repo is “new-to-you” if repos.first_seen_at >= now - N days (default N=7)

For the Today board, prefer:

repo_searches.last_seen_at = today

AND repos.first_seen_at >= today_start (for “new today”) OR last 7 days (for “new this week”)

Sorting:

primary: repos.stargazers_count DESC

secondary: repos.pushed_at DESC

B) “Rising” selection (stars delta)

Definition:

delta = stars(today) − stars(on_or_before(today - N days))

Use the closest snapshot on or before the target date.

If baseline snapshot missing, delta is NULL; exclude from rising list.

Sorting:

primary: delta DESC

secondary: stars(today) DESC

Default filters (anti-giant):

stars(today) BETWEEN 50 AND 20000 (configurable)

C) “Updated” selection

Definition:

repos.pushed_at >= now - 30 days (configurable)

Apply anti-giant stars range (same as above) unless user disables.

Saved searches: guardrails (agent must implement)

Add optional fields in saved_searches.json schema (backward compatible):

label (display label)

query (existing)

mode_defaults (optional): recommended stars range, recency window

exclude_known (optional): list of repo full_names to hard exclude (e.g., transformers/langchain)

Rules:

If these fields aren’t present, existing behavior remains unchanged.

Don’t require config changes to run.

Summarization spec (exact)
Eligibility (must follow)

A repo is eligible for summarization if:

It is on today board (repo_searches.last_seen_at = today), AND

It is either:

New-to-you in last 7 days, OR

In top K rising repos today (K configurable), OR

Manually pinned (optional future, stub allowed)

Daily cap:

Summarize at most MAX_SUMMARIES_PER_DAY (default 30)

Idempotency rules:

If repo_summaries exists for repo and updated_at is within last 14 days AND repo metadata hasn’t materially changed, skip.
Material change heuristic (choose one):

repos.pushed_at changed since last summary, OR

stars increased by ≥ X (e.g. 500), OR

description/topics changed (if tracked)

Input to model (Phase 1: metadata only)

Use only:

full_name, description, topics, language, stars, pushed_at, license (if present), homepage

Output format (must validate)

summary: 2–3 sentences

why_interesting: exactly 1 sentence

tags: JSON array of 3–6 short strings

Hard validation:

tags must be valid JSON array

no empty strings

enforce max length (e.g., summary <= 600 chars)

Store in repo_summaries.

Phase 2 (optional, behind feature flag)

fetch README only for eligible repos

source becomes "readme+metadata"

UI requirements (must implement)

On list items, if summary exists, render:

summary

why_interesting

tags (chips/badges)

Add controls:

Mode: New / Rising / Updated (default New)

Timeframe: 24h / 7d / 30d (default 7d)

Keep current “Today’s picks from saved searches” concept intact.

